    """Given the maximum levels of nesting of each parent and maximum level of nesting of each son, calculate
    the maximum level of nesting for the parent.

    The logic is: Given the maximum levels of nesting for the son, find the minimum of the level of each son.
    This minimum is the maximum depth at which we can be at to consider a parent at level max_depth_son.
    If max_depth_son > max_depth_parent, then no matter how deep a son is it cannot contribute to the max depth.
    Otherwise, the parent is at a level >= min of its children.
    """
    res = 0
    for x in p_son_list:
        res = max(res, x)
    return res


